draw((0,-1)--(0,1));
draw((-1.5,0)--(1.2,0)^^(0,0)--(sqrt(.96),0)^^(0,0)--(-sqrt(.96),0)^^(0,.24)--(sqrt(.96),0^^(sqrt(.96,0)--(0,.24)--(-sqrt(.96),0)^^(sqrt(.96,0)--(0,-.24)--(-sqrt(.96),0));
label("$x$",(1.5,0),E);
label("$y$",(0,1.2),N);
label("$\cdot$", (sqrt(.96),0), S); label("$\cdot$", (-sqrt(.96),0), S);
label("$(0,r)$",(0,.24),W); label("$(0,-r)$",(0,-.24),W);
[/asy] We see that the distances from $(0,r)$ to the two circles are $\sqrt{r^2 - 1}$ and $r - \sqrt{r^2 - 1}.$ It follows that $2(r - \sqrt{r^2 - 1}) = 2\sqrt{r^2 - 1},$ so $$r - \sqrt{r^2 - 1} = \sqrt{r^2 - 1}.$$Thus \[2r^2 - 2r\sqrt{r^2 - 1} = 0,\]which leads us to $r(\sqrt{r^2 - 1} - r) = 0.$ This leaves us with $r = \boxed{\sqrt{2}}.$ </think> <answer> \sqrt{2} </answer>

