The product of the visible numbers is the product of the numbers on all the faces of the die minus the number opposite to the face showing, which is the product of all 6 faces divided by this opposite number: $360 / \text{number opposite}$.  Because the opposite faces of a standard die add up to 7, the number opposite is greatest when the $3$ is visible, making the greatest common divisor of all the visible products $360/3 = \boxed{120}$.

